# LZ round trip

The input holds up to 24 seven-bit characters, one per u16 cell. Pass distinct
24-cell buffers for the packed stream and decoded output. The chain limit is
1–3. "'`compress` returns the number of packed cells. Pass that length to
`decompress`, which requires a valid stream that expands to at most 24 cells
and returns the number of decoded cells. `roundTrip` connects the two calls.

Each packed cell holds one byte.

| Bits | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `0ccccccc` | Emit the literal character `c` (0–127). |
| `1llddddd` | Copy `ll + 3` cells from `ddddd + 1` cells back. |

The compressor visits hash-chain links newest first and keeps the nearest
match on ties. It inserts all consumed positions that begin a complete
triple. The decoder copies forward, so a distance-one match can extend a
run by reading cells from earlier iterations of the same copy loop.

Run this in the workbench console with the project open to encode and decode
24 A cells on a fresh optimized program.

```js
wb.projects.current.run('"'explore');
"'```

The packed prefix is `[65, 224, 224, 224, 192]`. The script also returns all
24 decoded cells and the RV32 instruction count for the round trip.

The next console example encodes `AABBAAB` with one and two chain visits.

```js
const input = [65, 65, 66, 66, 65, 65, 66];
return [1, 2].map(limit => {
  const run = p.exec('"'compress', [input, Array(24).fill(0), limit]);
  return run.buffers[1].cells.slice(0, run.result);
});
"'```

One visit yields seven literals. Two visits yield `[65, 65, 66, 66, 131]`
because the older `AAB` matches at distance four after the newer `BAA`
collides in the same bucket.
